<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baji Rout</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1926–1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baji Rout was a 12-year-old boatman from Dhenkanal in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, who was shot dead by state police on 11 October 1938 for refusing to ferry them across the Brahmani river at Bhuban. The police were pursuing protesters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/praja-mandal">Praja Mandal</a> movement against the ruler of Dhenkanal. He is remembered in India as one of the youngest martyrs of the freedom movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baji-rout.jpg" alt="Baji Rout" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sidhartha Rath india · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baji_rout.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
